        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 8: Why It Matters -->
        <div class="section-heading-with-line">
          <h2>Why the Painterly Approach Matters</h2>
        </div>

        <p>Painterly photography slows the viewer down.</p>

        <p>Instead of rewarding a quick glance, it invites sustained attention. The image is not about what is immediately visible, but about what gradually emerges.</p>

        <p>At its best, the painterly approach lets the eye and brain suspend disbelief. The viewer stops thinking, <em>I am looking at a photograph of an event</em>, and begins to feel that a story is unfolding in front of them.</p>

        <p>In a crowded visual world, presence does not come from intensity or saturation. It comes from structure, tone, and restraint.</p>

        <p>When technique recedes, story begins.</p>

        <section class="faq-block" aria-labelledby="painterly-faq-heading">
